"""Scheduled US macro release dates for the announcement-premium sleeve.

Every date is the day the number was PUBLISHED (the market-moving day), taken
from the primary source on 2026-09-24:

- FOMC: the statement/decision day (last day) of each *scheduled* meeting,
  federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm and the
  fomchistoricalYYYY.htm pages. Excluded: unscheduled meetings (2020-03-03,
  2020-03-15), the cancelled 2020-03-17/18 meeting, and the 2025-08-22
  notation vote on the policy framework. 2026-12-09 and 2027 are the
  published forward schedule (tentative until confirmed).
- EMPLOYMENT (Employment Situation, 08:30 ET), CPI (08:30 ET), PPI (08:30 ET):
  release dates parsed from the BLS archived-news-release filenames
  (bls.gov/bls/news-release/{empsit,cpi,ppi}.htm, files are named
  <release>_MMDDYYYY) plus the forward schedule pages
  (bls.gov/schedule/news_release/<release>.htm) for the rest of 2026.
  Gaps are real: the Oct-2013 and Oct/Nov-2025 government shutdowns delayed
  or cancelled releases.

Usage: announcement_days(["FOMC", "CPI"]) -> DatetimeIndex of release days.
For an 08:30 release the premium accrues 16:00 (d-1) -> 09:30 (d); for the
14:00 FOMC statement it accrues through the day of d.
"""
